11: def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
12:     """
13:     Overlay the four separated 4x4 panels into one 4x4 image using a fixed front-to-back panel order.
14: 
15:     Input structure
16:     - The input is a 4x19 grid split by three full-height separator columns into four 4x4 panels.
17:     - Each panel contains background 0 plus exactly one foreground color, and the four panel colors are distinct.
18: 
19:     Rule
20:     - Treat 0 cells in each panel as transparent.
21:     - Stack the panels front-to-back in positional order: third panel, fourth panel, first panel, second panel.
22:     - The output cell is the first non-background color visible at that position, or 0 if all panels are empty there.
23: 
24:     Key insight
25:     - The four masks are already aligned; the only hidden information is their layer priority, which starts at the third panel and then proceeds cyclically.
26:     """
